---
// Pillar two: the machine you can hand to an agent. Headings are the jobs, not
// the features, and every one maps to a command that ships in the image. The
// limit is stated on the page, not buried: rollback covers the OS, never the
// home folder -- docs/AGENTS-SAFETY.md is the long version, linked below.
import { REPO } from '../data/site';

const JOBS = [
  {
    t: 'It reads the manual first',
    d: 'The image ships a briefing for coding agents: tools go in a toolbox, apps are Flatpaks, never reboot, and what rollback does and doesn’t undo. pulsar agents-md prints it, and setup puts it where each agent already looks.',
  },
  {
    t: 'Add an agent in one line',
    d: 'Claude Code, Codex, Gemini, opencode or aider, each installed into its own toolbox and run from any terminal. None ships by default, and one you installed yourself is left alone.',
  },
  {
    t: 'Something broke? Paste one thing',
    d: 'pulsar report gathers health checks, failed services, recent warnings, the GPU and Flatpak state into one document, with your hostname, username and addresses taken out.',
  },
  {
    t: 'Run models on your own GPU',
    d: 'On the NVIDIA image, any container can ask for the graphics card by name. A small model generated 307 tokens a second on the GPU, 58 on the CPU.',
  },
  {
    t: 'Let it try things',
    d: 'The system is read-only and every change to it is a new version you can boot out of. A bad update rolls itself back before you notice.',
  },
];

const EXAMPLE = [
  'pulsar setup agent claude',
  'pulsar report --text',
  'podman run --device nvidia.com/gpu=all IMAGE',
].join('\n');
---

<section class="chapter" id="agents">
  <h2>The safest machine to hand to an agent</h2>
  <arc-divider class="h-rule" align="left" variant="line-gradient"></arc-divider>
  <p class="lede">
    An agent on Pulsar can build, test and experiment all day.
    {' '}<span class="sent">The one thing it cannot do is leave you with a broken&nbsp;system.</span>
  </p>

  <div class="split">
    <dl class="jobs">
      {
        JOBS.map((j) => (
          <div class="job">
            <dt>{j.t}</dt>
            <dd>{j.d}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>
    <div class="side">
      <arc-code-block class="theme-fixed-dark" language="bash" filename="terminal" code={EXAMPLE}></arc-code-block>
      <p class="limit">
        <strong>What it can’t protect:</strong> your home folder. Rollback covers the operating
        system, not your files, so git and backups still do their usual job.{' '}
        <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/docs/AGENTS-SAFETY.md`}>Exactly what an agent can and can’t touch&nbsp;→</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .split {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 7fr) minmax(0, 5fr);
    gap: var(--space-2xl);
    align-items: start;
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }
  .jobs {
    margin: 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }
  .job {
    padding: var(--space-md) 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }
  .job:first-child {
    border-top: 0;
    padding-top: 0;
  }
  dt {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: var(--font-display-weight);
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
  }
  dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .side {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    position: sticky;
    top: calc(var(--space-3xl) + var(--space-md));
  }
  .side arc-code-block {
    display: block;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .limit {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .limit strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  .limit a {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: var(--space-xs);
  }
  @media (max-width: 56rem) {
    .split {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--space-xl);
    }
    .side {
      position: static;
    }
  }
</style>
